{
  "id": "commonsense-psychology",
  "term": "commonsense psychology",
  "definition": "Commonsense psychology here means the everyday assumptions people use to make sense of group life. In this context, it refers to the tendency to infer that members who are more respected are also more typical of the group, and vice versa, especially when the group seems cohesive.",
